ew turnaround is externally\n122\t  controlled and cannot be compressed; by explicit HLR-1 statement it blocks\n123\t  all shipping work. Recorded here rather than as an acceptance criterion.\n124\t\n125\t## Tiered Delivery\n126\t\n127\tEvaluated per Step 5.5 for the legal-clearance dependency with uncertain\n128\ttiming: the strategy states the clearance \"blocks all shipping work,\" and no\n129\timplementation epic delivers user-visible value without a productized store.\n130\tTier 1 is therefore the risk-reduction work only (the legal investigation\n131\titself); all productization, integration, and defaults work is Tier 2,\n132\tdependency-gated. No partial-value split is viable.\n133\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-95589ff7a1343953","agent_id":"a56a5d62b8da93dbe","session_id":"aee89738-3ddf-45ac-bec8-585fb72c96b4","uuid":"22ee6ad9-3eb1-4da8-a911-a01287458579","timestamp":"2026-10-22T17:01:16.648Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a03f0c3c27dc86ed","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9012 decomposition"}
