{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5393f4c6bd01a4b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9012-E005\n3\ttitle: Platform Operator enablement of the bundled S3-compatible object store\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9012\n5\tcomponent: Platform Operator\n6\tteam: RHOAI Platform Operator\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9012-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9012-E003\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9012-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: Integrate the Apache-2.0 fallback upstream instead of MinIO;\n16\t    the enablement surface is unchanged but the bundled store, its configuration surface,\n17\t    and upgrade lifecycle are reworked.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 0\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Medium\n31\tai_implementability_score: 2\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Platform Operator enablement of the bundled S3-compatible object store\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tDelivers the core capability of the strategy: administrators can enable a\n40\tsupported, bundled S3-compatible object store through the Platform Operator,\n41\twith productized images and an upgrade lifecycle. The store is opt-in,\n42\ttargeting disconnected and PoC clusters where no customer-provided\n43\tS3-compatible storage exists.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Platform Operator support for deploying and enabling the bundled object\n48\t  store chosen by the legal clearance decision.\n49\t- Opt-in enablement: the store is disabled by default; clusters without the\n50\t  capability enabled are unchanged, and customer-provided S3 configurations\n51\t  continue to work unchanged.\n52\t- Definition of how the bundled store is exposed to platform components\n53\t  (endpoint and credential discovery) so consuming components can target it\n54\t  without manual endpoint configuration.\n55\t- Upgrade lifecycle: the operator manages version upgrades of the bundled\n56\t  store.\n57\t- A clean disable/rollback path for the capability.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- An administrator can enable the bundled S3-compatible object store through\n62\t  the Platform Operator, and the store becomes usable in the cluster.\n63\t- Enablement is opt-in: with the capability disabled, cluster behavior is\n64\t  unchanged and existing customer-provided storage configurations are\n65\t  unaffected.\n66\t- The bundled store runs the productized image, referenced by digest once\n67\t  the image build pipeline produces it.\n68\t- The Konflux build pipeline for the bundled store image is green.\n69\t- The operator upgrades the bundled store across product versions without\n70\t  requiring a full reinstall.\n71\t- The capability can be disabled and re-enabled cleanly.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- HLR-2 (P0): Administrators can enable a supported, bundled S3-compatible\n76\t  object store through the Platform Operator, with productized images and\n77\t  upgrade lifecycle.\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-95589ff7a1343953","agent_id":"a56a5d62b8da93dbe","session_id":"aee89738-3ddf-45ac-bec8-585fb72c96b4","uuid":"6950c929-2ad5-435b-a30a-8c52cf8d418b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T17:01:35.154Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5393f4c6bd01a4b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9012 decomposition"}
