1\t  continue to work unchanged.\n52\t- Definition of how the bundled store is exposed to platform components\n53\t  (endpoint and credential discovery) so consuming components can target it\n54\t  without manual endpoint configuration.\n55\t- Upgrade lifecycle: the operator manages version upgrades of the bundled\n56\t  store.\n57\t- A clean disable/rollback path for the capability.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- An administrator can enable the bundled S3-compatible object store through\n62\t  the Platform Operator, and the store becomes usable in the cluster.\n63\t- Enablement is opt-in: with the capability disabled, cluster behavior is\n64\t  unchanged and existing customer-provided storage configurations are\n65\t  unaffected.\n66\t- The bundled store runs the productized image, referenced by digest once\n67\t  the image build pipeline produces it.\n68\t- The Konflux build pipeline for the bundled store image is green.\n69\t- The operator upgrades the bundled store across product versions without\n70\t  requiring a full reinstall.\n71\t- The capability can be disabled and re-enabled cleanly.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- HLR-2 (P0): Administrators can enable a supported, bundled S3-compatible\n76\t  object store through the Platform Operator, with productized images and\n77\t  upgrade lifecycle.\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8de228d23f83b6ea","agent_id":"abb987687b7cc5825","session_id":"aee89738-3ddf-45ac-bec8-585fb72c96b4","uuid":"a98e9ad4-848e-4854-9b9a-87c23b9802fc","timestamp":"2026-10-22T17:06:14.466Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0c15aff57471cc5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9012 decomposition"}
