rnally\n121\t  controlled and cannot be compressed; by explicit HLR-1 statement it blocks\n122\t  all shipping work. Recorded here rather than as an acceptance criterion.\n123\t\n124\t## Tiered Delivery\n125\t\n126\tEvaluated per Step 5.5 for the legal-clearance dependency with uncertain\n127\ttiming: the strategy states the clearance \"blocks all shipping work,\" and no\n128\timplementation epic delivers user-visible value without a productized store.\n129\tTier 1 is therefore the risk-reduction work only (the legal investigation\n130\titself); all productization, integration, and defaults work is Tier 2,\n131\tdependency-gated. No partial-value split is viable.\n132\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8de228d23f83b6ea","agent_id":"abb987687b7cc5825","session_id":"aee89738-3ddf-45ac-bec8-585fb72c96b4","uuid":"5668ce38-25d3-412f-9b54-52ddf037886c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T17:06:16.640Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b04cbd710693e7af","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9012 decomposition"}
