{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e03dcd605a92d93","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9012\n3\tepic_count: 8\n4\tcritical_path_length: 5\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9012\n11\t\n12\t**Strategy**: Bundle an S3-compatible object store for disconnected installs\n13\t**Triage**: full decomposition — not below-threshold (spans multiple components\n14\tand teams, and contains a genuine unknown whose answer changes what the\n15\tproductization epics build) and not docs-only (code and productization work\n16\trequired).\n17\t\n18\t## Epic List\n19\t\n20\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n21\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n22\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E001 | Legal clearance for redistributing the bundled object store (AGPL-3.0) | Investigation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n23\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E002 | Midstream repo onboarding for the bundled object store | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n24\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E003 | License validation for the bundled object store's transitive dependencies | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E004 | Konflux build pipeline onboarding for the bundled object store image | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E005 | Platform Operator enablement of the bundled S3-compatible object store | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E006 | Data Science Pipelines connection defaults for the bundled object store | Implementation | RHOAI Pipelines | P1 |\n28\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E007 | Model serving connection defaults for the bundled object store | Implementation | RHOAI Serving | P1 |\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E008 | Documentation for the bundled object store | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n30\t\n31\t## Dependency DAG\n32\t\n33\t```mermaid\n34\tgraph TD\n35\t    RHAISTRAT-9012-E001 --> RHAISTRAT-9012-E002\n36\t    RHAISTRAT-9012-E001 --> RHAISTRAT-9012-E003\n37\t    RHAISTRAT-9012-E001 --> RHAISTRAT-9012-E005\n38\t    RHAISTRAT-9012-E002 --> RHAISTRAT-9012-E004\n39\t    RHAISTRAT-9012-E003 --> RHAISTRAT-9012-E005\n40\t    RHAISTRAT-9012-E005 --> RHAISTRAT-9012-E006\n41\t    RHAISTRAT-9012-E005 --> RHAISTRAT-9012-E007\n42\t    RHAISTRAT-9012-E002 --> RHAISTRAT-9012-E008\n43\t    RHAISTRAT-9012-E003 --> RHAISTRAT-9012-E008\n44\t    RHAISTRAT-9012-E004 --> RHAISTRAT-9012-E008\n45\t    RHAISTRAT-9012-E005 --> RHAISTRAT-9012-E008\n46\t    RHAISTRAT-9012-E006 --> RHAISTRAT-9012-E008\n47\t    RHAISTRAT-9012-E007 --> RHAISTRAT-9012-E008\n48\t```\n49\t\n50\t## DAG Justification\n51\t\n52\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n53\t|------|------|-----------|\n54\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 3 (Investigation gate) | The legal clearance outcome selects the upstream (MinIO vs. Apache-2.0 fallback); repo onboarding is a true gate with `rewrite` impact. |\n55\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 3 (Investigation gate) | The dependency tree to be scanned depends on which upstream is selected; `rewrite` on fallback. |\n56\t| E001 → E005 | Rule 3 (Investigation gate) | The operator integration scope (which store is bundled) is directly rewritten if the fallback upstream is selected. |\n57\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 5 (repo-onboarding → konflux-onboarding serial) | The Konflux build pipeline needs the midstream repository to exist. |\n58\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 9 (license-validation → general implementation serial) | If license validation fails, the dependency set changes and the approach changes. |\n59\t| (no edge) E004 ↔ E005 | Rule 10 (konflux-onboarding ∥ general implementation) | Konflux onboarding and the operator implementation run in parallel; coupling is enforced by the \"build pipeline green\" and \"pinned image digest\" acceptance criteria on the implementation epic, never by a DAG edge. |\n60\t| (no edge) E002 → E005 | Rule 6 / Rule 13 note | The operator work lives in the Platform Operator repo (repo-onboarding does not block other repos); the productized image digest is a configuration reference filled in at execution time — an AC gate, not a DAG edge. |\n61\t| E005 → E006 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The operator epic defines how the bundled store is exposed (endpoint/credential discovery); the pipelines defaults build against that contract. |\n62\t| E005 → E007 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | Same exposure contract consumed by the model serving defaults. |\n63\t| E002, E003, E004, E005, E006, E007 → E008 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation is blocked by every Implementation epic; it describes what was built. These edges do not trigger priority inheritance (docs-authoring exception). |\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n66\t\n67\t| HLR | Priority | Epics |\n68\t|-----|----------|-------|\n69\t| HLR-1 | P0 | E001 |\n70\t| HLR-2 | P0 | E002, E003, E004, E005 |\n71\t| HLR-3 | P1 | E006, E007 |\n72\t| HLR-4 | P2 | E008 |\n73\t\n74\tFull coverage: every HLR maps to at least one epic; no orphaned requirements.\n75\t\n76\t## Investigation Outcome Modeling\n77\t\n78\tThe legal clearance has two bounded outcomes: (A) AGPL-3.0 redistribution of\n79\tMinIO is cleared; (B) terms cannot be satisfied and the Apache-2.0 fallback\n80\t(e.g. SeaweedFS) is selected. Both outcomes yield the same epic structure —\n81\tthe same onboarding chain, operator integration, connection defaults, and\n82\tdocumentation — with the productization epics' scope rewritten to the\n83\tselected upstream. The outcome is therefore modeled as `gated_by` +\n84\t`gate_failure_impact: rewrite` gates on the directly affected epics (E002,\n85\tE003, E005) rather than conditional branch epics: no epic exists in one\n86\toutcome but not the other, and downstream epics (connection defaults,\n87\tdocumentation) are upstream-agnostic.\n88\t\n89\t## Component Mapping Notes\n90\t\n91\t- The bundled object store 