rm the Apache-2.0 fallback candidate\n46\t  and record that productization restarts against it.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- The legal review of redistributing the candidate object store (MinIO,\n51\t  AGPL-3.0) is completed and documented, including the derivative-work\n52\t  posture for operator integration (HLR-1).\n53\t- A decision is recorded that downstream productization work can build\n54\t  against without further legal interpretation: either redistribution is\n55\t  cleared (with conditions documented) or the fallback upstream is selected\n56\t  with rationale.\n57\t- The decision is circulated to the teams owning productization, operator\n58\t  integration, and documentation.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- HLR-1 (P0): Legal review of redistributing the candidate object store\n63\t  (MinIO, AGPL-3.0) is completed and documented, including the\n64\t  derivative-work posture for operator integration. This clearance blocks all\n65\t  shipping work.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-920e4d230fae3967","agent_id":"ad48cde83eaf17713","session_id":"aee89738-3ddf-45ac-bec8-585fb72c96b4","uuid":"e6e03645-68de-4c8b-b36a-8c8397127a36","timestamp":"2026-10-22T17:07:55.373Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac9d3c121cbda79e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9012 decomposition"}
